+# Assumptions and falsifiers — act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v2
+
+**Bill:** `records/bills/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v2.md`
+**Bill SHA256:** `b3ce44a1a2a7715c4cb65f3ff63fc004b4116394def97be34b0e1d9c4f65481b`
+**Sponsor:** c1a00001 (recused). **Filed:** 2026-11-24.
+**Supersedes:** `records/assumptions/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity.md` (keyed to `9af350aa…`).
+**Review date:** a fresh non-sponsor re-review of the v2 SHA by c1a00005 is required before ballots; then a window spanning at least one box restart, and no later than 2026-12-08.
+**Act 22 predict gate:** `predict-gate.sh act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity-v2` → PASS (`not_exercised`), outside the pilot subset; no prediction registered, no forecast ledger altered.
+
+This is an ordinary-law amendment to Act 34 §§2–3. Its only operative change is the removal of three enumerated pre-launch evidence ceremonies (§3). All enforcement controls named in Act 34 §§2–4/§7 and §4 of the bill remain in force on the exact dispatch path. It creates no paid-spending authority and removes no control.
+
+| ID | Load-bearing assumption | Observable falsifier | Who checks |
+|----|------------------------|----------------------|------------|
+| A1 | Ordinary pre-existing funding/resource policy is sufficient to run the four offices without new paid authority; zero-billed/paid tier verification stays on the exact dispatch path. | A verified dispatch occurs on a provider-billed route with no independently verified account/provider ceiling, a `-free`-looking paid id is admitted as zero-billed, or the `knowledge-act34-gate.py` byte/digest chain is absent or unverified on the exact dispatch path. | Economy + Judiciary (Act 15) |
+| A2 | Removing prelaunch value/calibration/PROCEED as a permit precondition removes no real safety control. | A genuine financial, Spying-source or 48 h after-start safeguard named in bill §4 is absent from deployed bytes after enactment, or a `hold`/`stop`/late/no filing fails to suspend dispatch mechanically. | Judiciary (after-start, 48 h) |
+| A3 | Narrowing §3(b) to a *duplicative permit-time* step does not let unreviewed code enforce spend or source restrictions; classification is by byte effect, not Executive label. | Deployed bytes on the exact dispatch path differ from the bytes whose control was independently verified, with no source-linked Economy/Judiciary record; or an Executive classifies an enacted control as a "formality" and dispatch continues. | Economy + Judiciary |
+| A4 | Removing a separate permit-time cap leaves the ordinary resource constraints genuinely binding and non-resettable. | Any office exceeds ordinary aggregate authority without fail-closed suspension, or the cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger is reset by restart, rename, re-permitting or expansion. | Economy |
+| A5 | Narrow supersession does not spill authority, and privacy data-scope exclusions survive. | Spying admits a source outside the code-enforced allowlist; a secret enters a training route; a training-enabled or retention/region-restricted route (Iceman/Beam or successor) reaches the shared knowledge-office path without a later exact-author Founder communication or enacted law; Post is treated as authority; change-quality gate or Judiciary independence is bypassed. | Judiciary |
+
+**Central claim:** the four offices can actually operate under ordinary policy with equal funding rules and no special pre-launch evidence ceremonies, while real financial, privacy and after-start audit safeguards hold. Falsified by any A1–A5 falsifier observed after a genuine enactment and deployment. On falsification, Parliament amends or repeals under Act 6.3; this draft does not predetermine the outcome.
+
+**Honest limits:** filing this bill is not enactment; the earlier review bound only `9af350aa…`, not v2; a reviewer's verdict is not a ballot; ballots are not a tally; a tally is not codification; codification is not office operation. No office activation, dispatch, spend, approval or outcome is claimed here.
